-## 17. Upcoming roadmap-owned seams
+## 17. Built-in agent role: `explorer` prompt
+
+The built-in `explorer` role already had an upstream registry seam and an empty embedded TOML stub.
+This fork fills that stub with a paraphrased read-only exploration prompt, sets low reasoning effort,
+and explicitly clears fallback project-doc filenames so the role stays lightweight and focused. The
+role wiring in `role.rs` remains a read-only reference; the patch surface is limited to the TOML body
+and its invariant coverage.
+
+| File | Role |
+|------|------|
+| `core/src/agent/builtins/explorer.toml` | Fork-filled built-in role config. Carries provenance on line 1, a `# SANDBOX PATCH:` marker on line 2, `model_reasoning_effort = "low"`, substantial `developer_instructions`, and `project_doc_fallback_filenames = []`. |
+| `core/src/agent/role_tests.rs` | Guards the changed role behavior and embedded TOML invariants. The changed and new test functions carry `// SANDBOX PATCH:` markers. |
+| `core/src/agent/role.rs::configs` | Read-only reference: `explorer` remains registered with `config_file: Some("explorer.toml")`. No edit. |
+| `core/src/agent/role.rs::config_file_contents` | Read-only reference: embeds `builtins/explorer.toml` through the existing `include_str!` match arm. No edit. |
+
+Important invariants:
+
+- `core/src/agent/builtins/explorer.toml` must parse as `ConfigToml`; `include_str!` embeds bytes but
+  does not validate TOML syntax at compile time.
+- `developer_instructions` must stay non-blank after trim and at least 200 characters, so the built-in
+  role cannot silently regress to an empty or placeholder prompt.
+- `project_doc_fallback_filenames = []` must remain an explicit top-level TOML array that
+  deserializes to `project_doc_fallback_filenames == Some(vec![])`. Do not replace this with a
+  typed `ConfigToml` default check; the raw TOML key is the invariant.
+- Applying the role must preserve the caller's model while setting `model_reasoning_effort` to `Low`
+  and adding exactly one session-flags layer.
+- Preserve the `# SANDBOX PATCH:` marker in `explorer.toml` and the `// SANDBOX PATCH:` markers on the
+  changed/new test function lines.
+
+Rebase guidance: if upstream leaves `explorer.toml` empty, keep this fork-filled body and its markers.
+If upstream adds its own `explorer.toml` content, merge upstream's functional additions only after a
+fresh license/paraphrase review of the combined prompt body, then re-run the focused role tests. If
+upstream moves the built-in role registry, re-locate the `explorer.toml` include seam before changing
+tests; do not add a second registry path.
+
+---
